+## Entries from `adconnect-migration` Phase 2-4 (closed 2026-05-12)
+
+### AdConnect `make_get_current_user_org(required=False)` divergence from ERP/PF (`required=True`)
+
+- **Subject:** `products/adconnect/backend/app/dependencies.py` calls `make_get_current_user_org(..., required=False)` whereas the canonical references (ERP-imobiliario / personal-finance / youtube-crawler) pin `required=True`.
+- **Decision:** keep `required=False` at AdConnect for now.
+- **Reason:** AdConnect is single-instance brand-bounded; the `DEFAULT_ORG_ID` fallback in routers preserves V1 behavior where many `MockUser` test paths intentionally omit `org_id` user-metadata. Flipping to `required=True` would 403 every such test path without changing production behavior (production tokens always carry `org_id`). The divergence is a test-surface accommodation, not a production-policy gap.
+- **Scope:** `products/adconnect/backend/app/dependencies.py` only.
+- **Revisit trigger:** **AdConnect ships multi-brand multi-tenancy** (MVP §4 deferred work) — at that point `required=True` becomes a correctness gate, not a test-surface compromise; the migration also lifts the `DEFAULT_ORG_ID` fallback. OR **a second product surfaces the same `required=False` need** → N=2 fires recurrence; lift the test-shape pattern to a `MockUser` defaults convention in `noctusai_lib.testing` so the auth-dep stays `required=True` everywhere.
+- **Recorded by:** `projects/adconnect-migration/PROJECT.md` Phase 2 close (Engineer ADCO-MIG-P2, 2026-05-11), re-confirmed at Phase 4 close (Engineer ACMI-P4, 2026-05-12).
+
+### AdConnect `dependencies.py` reuses `app.database._db` (vs constructing its own `DatabaseModule`)
+
+- **Subject:** `products/adconnect/backend/app/dependencies.py` does `from . import database` and consumes `database._db.get_client` rather than the canonical pattern of constructing a fresh `DatabaseModule()` instance and binding it to the seed factory.
+- **Decision:** keep the reuse pattern at AdConnect for now.
+- **Reason:** AdConnect's `tests/conftest.py` patches `app.database._db.get_client` (and friends) directly at module-attribute level — a legacy pattern from the MVP wave. Constructing a second `DatabaseModule` instance inside `dependencies.py` would create an instance the conftest patches never touch, so 145+ tests resolve against the real Supabase client and crash. ERP/PF avoid this by patching only the framework class level (`noctusai_seed.database.DatabaseModule.get_client`). The reuse pattern is structurally a test-coupling artifact, not a runtime defect.
+- **Scope:** `products/adconnect/backend/app/dependencies.py` + the patches in `products/adconnect/backend/tests/conftest.py` (lines 214-222) + `products/adconnect/backend/tests/routers/test_admin_router.py` (lines 65-70, 81-86).
+- **Revisit trigger:** **a second product surfaces the same conftest module-attr patching pattern** → N=2 fires recurrence; lift `MockSupabaseClient`-binding convention to bind at class level only, drop module-attr patches everywhere. OR **AdConnect's conftest gets migrated to class-level patching** (a focused sub-project) → the `app.database._db` reuse retires; `dependencies.py` constructs its own `DatabaseModule()` matching the canonical shape.
+- **Recorded by:** `projects/adconnect-migration/PROJECT.md` Phase 2 close (Engineer ADCO-MIG-P2, 2026-05-11), re-confirmed at Phase 4 close (Engineer ACMI-P4, 2026-05-12).
+
+### AdConnect router helpers `_resolve_org_id` / `_resolve_distributor_id` / `_is_admin` duplicated N=5
+
+- **Subject:** five AdConnect routers (`cart.py` / `orders.py` / `products.py` / `financial.py` / `distributors.py`) carry byte-similar private helpers — `_resolve_org_id(user, org_id)` (N=5), `_resolve_distributor_id(user)` (N=4), `_is_admin(user)` (N=2). Surfaced in Phase 2's post-refactor diff because the canonical `(user, token, org_id)` triple destructure made the per-router helpers visible side-by-side. The recurrence rule fires (N=5 > N=3).
+- **Decision:** defer the absorption — keep helpers per-router for now, file follow-up project `adconnect-router-auth-helper-absorption` for the lift.
+- **Reason:** the test infrastructure is currently broken across all products in worktrees (conftest's `purge_shadowing_editable_finders` drops the `noctusai_seed` editable finder when the host venv's editable install points at a sibling worktree — see Phase 4 findings). Refactoring 5 routers without a working test baseline risks regressions. The helpers are byte-similar but not byte-identical (orders helper accepts admin shortcut; financial helper threads `auth_org_id`), so the absorption needs careful test coverage. Once the test infrastructure regression is fixed, the lift becomes a 1-2 hour focused project — target shape: a single `_auth_helpers.py` module beside `dependencies.py` exporting the three helpers, mirroring how ERP/PF would do it canonically.
+- **Scope:** `products/adconnect/backend/app/routers/{cart,orders,products,financial,distributors}.py` (helpers at the top of each file, ~6-12 LoC each).
+- **Revisit trigger:** **the test-infrastructure regression is fixed** (architect-followup from Phase 4) → file `adconnect-router-auth-helper-absorption` immediately. OR **a 6th router surfaces the same helper** (currently 4 of 9 routers don't carry it — `auth.py`, `rewards.py`, `sellout.py`, `admin.py`) → upgrade urgency from deferred to active.
+- **Recorded by:** `projects/adconnect-migration/PROJECT.md` Phase 4 close (Engineer ACMI-P4, 2026-05-12).
+
