+**Phase 4 verification limitation (surfaced as architect-followup):**
+- The brief required `pytest products/adconnect/backend/tests/ -k "not realdb" -p no:randomly` to assert baseline preserved (248 passing). **Result: 99 passed, 149 errors** — same failure mode on MAIN at HEAD `398169c` (verified from `/Users/rapha/Documents/repository/NoctusAI/noctusai/products/adconnect/backend/`). Same failure mode on `products/erp-imobiliario/backend/` (11 collection errors). **Root cause:** `purge_shadowing_editable_finders(_LIB)` in conftests (seeded by `noctusai_lib.testing.conftest_helpers`) drops BOTH `noctusai_lib` AND `noctusai_seed` editable finders because the host venv's editable installs point at the main worktree (`/seed/lib/backend` and `/seed/framework/backend` respectively). After purge, `noctusai_lib` resolves via the conftest's prepended `sys.path` entry pointing at the worktree-local `seed/lib/backend` — but `noctusai_seed` has NO replacement registration (the conftest only prepends `seed/lib/backend`, not `seed/framework/backend`). All tests using the `client` fixture fail at `patch("app.database._db.get_client")` with `AttributeError: module 'app' has no attribute 'database'` — because `app.database` import-chains through `noctusai_seed` (`from noctusai_seed import create_database_module`) and never completes. This is **pre-existing** and **environmental** — not caused by Phase 2/3 work; the Phase 1-3 close commit's "248 passing" claim must have been captured in a different environment state (likely with editable installs pointing at the close-commit's branch). See findings below.
 
